# The native projects are GENERATED, never committed.
#
# `cap add ios` / `cap add android` copy a template out of `@capacitor/{ios,android}` and then
# `cap sync` rewrites parts of it from `capacitor.config.json` and the installed plugins. A
# committed copy is a fork of that template that drifts silently from the Capacitor version in
# `package.json` — the whole class of bug where a store build works from an old checkout and
# nowhere else. Regenerate them with `npm run add:ios` / `npm run add:android` (see README.md).
/ios/
/android/

# CocoaPods and Gradle output, in case a platform dir is generated somewhere unexpected.
Pods/
.gradle/
local.properties

# Xcode / Android Studio local state
*.xcuserstate
xcuserdata/
*.iml
.idea/
